  "assessment": [
    {
      "topic": "Consent and capability",
      "locations": [
        "app/notifications.go:98",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:91-123",
        "specs/notifications.md"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Settings does not request authorization. Only the explicitly named permission method requests alert and sound. Notify queries authorization and refuses denied/not-determined without prompting. Darwin flags describe implemented transport, not current bundled/authorized/runtime availability; delivered acceptance is not a display guarantee."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Namespace and removal",
      "locations": [
        "app/notifications.go:63",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:13",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:56-61",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:124-129"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Validated caller IDs are prefixed in both delivery and withdrawal. Only supplied IDs are removed; no global remove-all path. The reservation is within the application notification center, and concurrent OS delivery/removal is explicitly not transactional."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Wire admission and ownership",
      "locations": [
        "app/notifications.go:43",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.go:26",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:27-55",
        "drivers/cogent/services_darwin.go:121-151"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Public byte caps precede UTF-8 validation, IDs and payload structure are independently validated by native parsing, the detached shared producer bounds/copies input before asynchronous consumption, and C-to-Go reply bounds precede copying. Native callback pools and exception-to-terminal-result handling are present."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Cancellation, credits, shutdown",
      "locations": [
        "drivers/cogent/services.go:30-63",
        "drivers/cogent/services_darwin.go:62-174",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:73-134"
      ],
      "conclusion": "The new branch inherits shared eight-credit admission, monotonic tokens and once-only terminal map removal. Origin context/application lifetime checks precede asynchronous actions and terminal publication. Cancellation releases the waiting caller but cannot undo executing authorization/delivery/removal; accepted credit is retained until native terminal acknowledgment or shutdown. The notification bridge does not install or replace a delegate."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Meaningful fixture scope",
      "locations": [
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin_test.go:22",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin_test.go:60",
        "drivers/cogent/notifications_darwin.m:137-150",
        "examples/sdk-contract/notifications_test.go"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Fixtures validate malformed/bounded wire, real content/request data objects, injected authorization enum normalization, shared producer ownership, actual C-to-Go permission error, optional service compatibility, and an in-memory public consumer. These fixtures do not access UNUserNotificationCenter, request permission, deliver, play sound, or alter settings."
    }
  ],
